// std/block.lin
// Block (tuple) operations for Lin.
//
// Blocks are built from nested `pair` calls:
//   (pair x y)                -> 2-element block: [x, y]
//   (pair x (pair y z))       -> 3-element block: [x, y, z]
//   (pair x (pair y (pair z w))) -> 4-element block: [x, y, z, w]
//
// Field access:
//   (blk)/1  -> first element
//   (blk)/2  -> second element (or rest of block for nested pairs)
//   (blk)/2/1 -> second element, first of rest  (third overall)
//   (blk)/2/2 -> second element, second of rest (fourth overall)
//
// `pair` is built into the lowering as a delta agent — no compiler
// changes needed. The type-directed dispatch rewrites binary `+` etc.
// to f32/f64 variants based on argument types; `pair` always creates
// a delta-(pair) node regardless of its argument types.
//
// Examples:
//   pos: (pair x (pair y z))       ; 3D position block
//   mat: (pair m0 (pair m1 ...))   ; arbitrary arity via nesting
//   first: (pos)/1                  ; x component
//   second: (pos)/2/1               ; y component
//   third: (pos)/2/2                 ; z component